WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.515 --> 00:00:02.893
- [Narrator] This is a billion dollars.

00:00:02.893 --> 00:00:03.755
We think.

00:00:03.755 --> 00:00:06.770
And that billion dollars
belongs to RJ Rappaport

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:08.824
and he's considered the "King of Cash."

00:00:08.824 --> 00:00:10.123
- "King of fake cash."

00:00:10.123 --> 00:00:13.373
- [Narrator] Okay, "King of Fake Cash."

00:00:14.857 --> 00:00:16.898
- My name is Rich "RJ" Rappaport

00:00:16.898 --> 00:00:19.922
and I'm the president of RJR Props.

00:00:19.922 --> 00:00:21.246
- [Narrator] Just a few years ago-

00:00:21.246 --> 00:00:22.907
- Actually it was nine years ago.

00:00:22.907 --> 00:00:25.125
- [Narrator] Oh sorry, nine years ago

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:27.277
RJR Props was born.

00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:29.417
It's a full service prop house,

00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:31.794
but it's specialty is cash.

00:00:31.794 --> 00:00:33.177
Fake cash.

00:00:33.177 --> 00:00:35.505
And there's only a few people
who can legally make it,

00:00:35.505 --> 00:00:37.338
and RJ is one of them.

00:00:40.722 --> 00:00:43.428
- We’ve worked with 50 Cent, Kendrick Lamar,

00:00:43.428 --> 00:00:46.302
Lil Wayne, Fat Joe, Young Dolph.

00:00:46.302 --> 00:00:48.211
- [Narrator] And that's
just to name a few.

00:00:48.211 --> 00:00:51.879
RJ's prop money has been used
in over 175 feature films,

00:00:51.879 --> 00:00:54.029
television shows, and music videos.

00:00:54.029 --> 00:00:55.779
And he devoted three full years

00:00:55.779 --> 00:00:59.930
to perfecting that crisp
green paper we call money.

00:00:59.930 --> 00:01:00.847
Prop money.

00:01:02.686 --> 00:01:04.526
- And we went down a long path,

00:01:04.526 --> 00:01:06.021
from working with the Secret Service

00:01:06.021 --> 00:01:07.605
and learning all the laws,

00:01:07.605 --> 00:01:09.331
to make sure that everyone that uses it,

00:01:09.331 --> 00:01:12.321
it will be legal for them
and it will look fantastic.

00:01:12.321 --> 00:01:14.044
- [Narrator] But for those
who don't follow the rules,

00:01:14.044 --> 00:01:16.450
they could wind up in big trouble.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:18.033
- There was a rash of arrests.

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:19.732
People were just literally jailed

00:01:19.732 --> 00:01:22.279
because they were using prop
money that looked too real.

00:01:22.279 --> 00:01:24.494
And I said to myself, "I'm
not going to touch this

00:01:24.494 --> 00:01:26.815
"unless I know I'm doing it legally."

00:01:26.815 --> 00:01:28.290
- [Narrator] Alongside the Secret Service,

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.851
RJ created two different
styles of prop money.

00:01:30.851 --> 00:01:32.568
One that is printed on both sides

00:01:32.568 --> 00:01:36.064
and is perfect for that
classic bank robbery scene.

00:01:36.064 --> 00:01:38.276
The other kind is so
close to the real deal,

00:01:38.276 --> 00:01:40.320
it can only be printed on one side.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.480
Otherwise, it could end up in circulation.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:45.021
It's designed for the
classic money shot, aka-

00:01:45.021 --> 00:01:45.854
- This.

00:01:45.854 --> 00:01:47.049
- [Narrator] The close up.

00:01:47.049 --> 00:01:48.153
- It's a tough business.

00:01:48.153 --> 00:01:49.503
We all work hard in it,

00:01:49.503 --> 00:01:52.654
and prop money especially is not easy.

00:01:52.654 --> 00:01:53.969
- [Narrator] Yeah, sounds like it.

00:01:53.969 --> 00:01:57.219
Thanks, RJ, for keeping fake money, real.

